From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:13:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 72/80] LOCAL: power: reset: qcom-pon: Set Motorola's
 bootloader flag

Motorola's bootloader enters fastboot after "reboot bootloader" only
when, besides the restart reason in SOFT_RB_SPARE, its "reboot_bl" bit
is set in DVDD_RB_SPARE (the downstream msm-poweroff stores
RESET_EXTRA_REBOOT_BL_REASON, BIT(2), there). With the optional
motorola,bootloader-spare-flag property, set those bits for the
mode-bootloader magic and clear them for every other mode.

LOCAL because the property has no binding; upstream this probably wants
a compatible-based quirk or a more generic description.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
---
 drivers/power/reset/qcom-pon.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/qcom-pon.c b/drivers/power/reset/qcom-pon.c
index 7e108982a..aa9b7d064 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/qcom-pon.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/qcom-pon.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <linux/reboot-mode.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 
+#define PON_DVDD_RB_SPARE		0x8d
 #define PON_SOFT_RB_SPARE		0x8f
 
 #define GEN1_REASON_SHIFT		2
@@ -25,6 +26,8 @@ struct qcom_pon {
 	u32 baseaddr;
 	struct reboot_mode_driver reboot_mode;
 	long reason_shift;
+	u32 bootloader_magic;
+	u32 bootloader_flag;
 };
 
 static int qcom_pon_reboot_mode_write(struct reboot_mode_driver *reboot,
@@ -41,6 +44,17 @@ static int qcom_pon_reboot_mode_write(struct reboot_mode_driver *reboot,
 	if (ret < 0)
 		dev_err(pon->dev, "update reboot mode bits failed\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * Some bootloaders (Motorola) only enter fastboot when an extra flag is
+	 * set in DVDD_RB_SPARE as well; keep it in step with the mode.
+	 */
+	if (!ret && pon->bootloader_flag)
+		ret = regmap_update_bits(pon->regmap,
+					 pon->baseaddr + PON_DVDD_RB_SPARE,
+					 pon->bootloader_flag,
+					 magic == pon->bootloader_magic ?
+					 pon->bootloader_flag : 0);
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -70,6 +84,12 @@ static int qcom_pon_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	reason_shift = (long)of_device_get_match_data(&pdev->dev);
 
 	if (reason_shift != NO_REASON_SHIFT) {
+		of_property_read_u32(pdev->dev.of_node, "mode-bootloader",
+				     &pon->bootloader_magic);
+		of_property_read_u32(pdev->dev.of_node,
+				     "motorola,bootloader-spare-flag",
+				     &pon->bootloader_flag);
+		pon->bootloader_flag &= 0xff;
 		pon->reboot_mode.dev = &pdev->dev;
 		pon->reason_shift = reason_shift;
 		pon->reboot_mode.write = qcom_pon_reboot_mode_write;
